<title>NETHERLANDS: PHILIPS TO INVEST $1.5 BLN IN ASIA - WSJ.</title>
<headline>PHILIPS TO INVEST $1.5 BLN IN ASIA - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics Asia Pacific Pte Ltd, part of Dutch group Philips Electronics , is to invest $1.5 billion in Asia over the next five years, the Wall Street Journal (Europe) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Quoting chairman Franciscus Sluiter, the WSJ said Philips' investments in Asia were part of the group's plan to double sales by 2000.</p>
<p>Sales in Asia hit $5.6 billion in the first nine months of this year, or 20 percent of total sales.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
